  "stem": "In right triangle \\(ABC\\), angle \\(C\\) is the right angle, and the measure of angle \\(A\\) is twice the measure of angle \\(B\\). What is the measure, in degrees, of angle \\(A\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "60"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "The two acute angles of a right triangle add to \\(90^{\\circ}\\). Let angle \\(B = b^{\\circ}\\); then angle \\(A = 2b^{\\circ}\\) and \\(2b + b = 90\\).",
    "\\(b = 30\\), so angle \\(A = 2(30) = 60^{\\circ}\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "b=symbols('b')\nbs=solve(Eq(2*b+b+90,180),b)[0]\nans=2*bs\nassert Rational(spr_answers[0])==ans==60\n",
